WEBVTT

00:03.160 --> 00:06.770
Fight for your justice,
show your courage.

00:06.770 --> 00:10.370
Right! Grasp truth in these hands.

00:10.370 --> 00:13.780
Fight for your justice, I want you

00:13.780 --> 00:21.200
as you fight through
with your head held up high.

00:35.860 --> 00:39.930
Rather than polishing diamonds

00:43.040 --> 00:46.970
give me a glistening future.

00:50.250 --> 00:52.480
Even if nothing's there, get up.

00:52.480 --> 00:56.350
It's important to turn on the switch.

00:57.450 --> 01:00.220
Something new that I don't want to yield.

01:00.220 --> 01:04.750
Seeking it is justice!

01:06.360 --> 01:09.930
Fight for your justice,
be serious about it.

01:09.930 --> 01:13.540
Right! Face reality head on.

01:13.540 --> 01:16.940
Fight for your justice,
I love how you

01:16.940 --> 01:27.340
never give up even if
the current is against you.

01:45.470 --> 01:48.530
I can't be chopped up by you guys!

01:52.870 --> 01:54.240
What's that?

02:01.920 --> 02:02.910
Dita!

02:19.170 --> 02:20.830
Damn you!

02:25.370 --> 02:27.030
What?

02:37.550 --> 02:40.020
S-Stop it...

02:43.290 --> 02:45.090
Stop it!

03:17.460 --> 03:18.790
That light...

03:21.330 --> 03:22.900
What was it?

03:22.900 --> 03:24.560
Mr. Alien.

03:27.900 --> 03:29.370
What, what?

03:29.370 --> 03:31.960
All of you together this early?

03:33.540 --> 03:35.780
It was trying to tell us something.

03:35.780 --> 03:39.280
At least, that's how I felt.

03:39.280 --> 03:41.820
Then... Then you guys saw it, too?

03:41.820 --> 03:45.050
So you also saw it, Mr. Alien?

03:45.050 --> 03:46.790
Creepy...

03:46.790 --> 03:50.760
All of us having the same dream is eerie.

03:50.760 --> 03:54.090
We share a common experience.

03:59.500 --> 04:03.640
The misshapen Dreads
and the Vanguard are proof.

04:03.640 --> 04:06.440
But still, a dream like that?

04:07.710 --> 04:08.680
Jura?

04:08.680 --> 04:09.740
I'm sorry.

04:09.740 --> 04:12.340
I'm going back to sleep.

04:19.290 --> 04:20.320
How's it going?

04:20.320 --> 04:20.990
Not good.

04:20.990 --> 04:23.390
The output is decreasing,
and the numbers aren't stabilizing.

04:23.390 --> 04:25.260
When did this start happening?

04:25.260 --> 04:27.260
About 10 minutes ago.

04:27.260 --> 04:29.830
This Paksis was the prototype.

04:29.830 --> 04:32.570
I can't begin to predict what'll happen.

04:32.570 --> 04:35.160
Geez! You're such a troublemaker!

04:41.410 --> 04:44.080
Still, that was strange.

04:44.080 --> 04:47.280
But it seemed so realistic...

04:47.280 --> 04:48.940
Mr. Alien!

04:50.080 --> 04:51.750
Found ya!

04:53.220 --> 04:55.720
What? You're scaring me.

04:55.720 --> 04:57.590
You still want something?

04:57.590 --> 05:00.160
Yeah. Um...

05:00.160 --> 05:04.270
I was wondering when you'd
come by and visit my room.

05:04.270 --> 05:07.100
Well, you promised, right?

05:07.100 --> 05:09.770
H-How can you say something like that?

05:09.770 --> 05:13.110
Like I can feel like
doing that right now!

05:13.110 --> 05:14.410
Then, when?

05:14.410 --> 05:15.640
Tomorrow?

05:15.640 --> 05:16.880
The day after?

05:16.880 --> 05:18.740
Or the day after that?

05:20.250 --> 05:23.120
Someday soon, all right?

05:23.120 --> 05:25.050
Wait, Mr. Alien.

05:25.050 --> 05:26.450
Then, then...

05:26.450 --> 05:28.120
Let's eat breakfast together!

05:28.120 --> 05:29.620
I'll eat by myself!

05:29.620 --> 05:30.960
Don't say that!

05:30.960 --> 05:34.860
- Oh, shut up!
- Come on, please, Mr. Alien?

05:34.860 --> 05:37.730
Today is another day.

05:37.730 --> 05:39.500
Hibiki and Dita...

05:39.500 --> 05:42.940
I can't believe she wants to chase men.
It makes me shiver, ribbit!

05:42.940 --> 05:46.440
Actually, that's normal.

05:46.440 --> 05:47.540
What're you thinking?

05:47.540 --> 05:50.280
Don't you think it's rude
to cross in front of a lady?

05:50.280 --> 05:51.380
But that's strange.

05:51.380 --> 05:53.810
You're a machine, and you're hiccuping.

05:58.050 --> 06:02.320
We've gotten to where
we are 90 days from Mejale.

06:02.320 --> 06:06.060
Concerning information of
Earth's plan to harvest organs...

06:06.060 --> 06:08.260
We've already sent communication pods...

06:08.260 --> 06:11.430
to our homeland of Mejale
and the men's planet of Tarak.

06:11.430 --> 06:15.700
What happened to the
message we sent before that?

06:15.700 --> 06:17.540
It should have arrived by now...

06:17.540 --> 06:21.440
but there still has been no
contact from Mejale or Tarak.

06:21.440 --> 06:23.410
Looks like we've been ignored.

06:23.410 --> 06:24.910
Well, of all things...

06:24.910 --> 06:29.250
the information we have this
time will turn them upside down.

06:29.250 --> 06:34.550
Especially since their objective
is to take our reproductive organs.

06:37.930 --> 06:39.560
Engine room, Parfet here!

06:39.560 --> 06:41.300
What's wrong, Parfet?

06:41.300 --> 06:42.530
Well...

06:42.530 --> 06:44.800
It's this morning's
abnormality in the Paksis...

06:44.800 --> 06:47.140
I have no idea what's causing it!

06:47.140 --> 06:50.470
We're continuing with
the control procedure...

06:50.470 --> 06:54.640
but the output is
down to 80% of normal.

06:54.640 --> 06:56.380
Geez, this again?

06:56.380 --> 06:58.550
Perhaps we still
show signs of rejection...

06:58.550 --> 07:02.050
from when the female ship
and the male ship fused together?

07:02.050 --> 07:05.090
I guess it's the same as us, right?

07:05.090 --> 07:10.190
The gap between men
and women is rather wide.

07:10.190 --> 07:11.520
Women are...

07:13.730 --> 07:16.860
eaters of men's internal
organs, so I hear.

07:16.860 --> 07:19.600
What are you reading, Duero?

07:19.600 --> 07:20.200
I found this in the cargo
bay of the pioneer ship.

07:20.200 --> 07:22.200
"Hello, Baby"
I found this in the cargo
bay of the pioneer ship.

07:22.200 --> 07:22.790
I found this in the cargo
bay of the pioneer ship.

07:25.570 --> 07:29.580
A baby begins when a father's seed,
called the sperm...

07:29.580 --> 07:34.080
is accepted by the mother's egg,
called an ovum.

07:34.080 --> 07:38.890
- The egg, now called a zygote...
- Is that interesting?

07:38.890 --> 07:41.080
Very interesting.

07:47.760 --> 07:50.160
Things sure have changed.

07:50.160 --> 07:52.130
Maybe we've gotten used to them.

07:52.130 --> 07:56.340
And it doesn't bother us that
much when we eat meals together.

07:56.340 --> 07:59.440
I used to believe
that men were all bacteria.

07:59.440 --> 08:03.480
But to be told suddenly that men
and women were both from Earth...

08:03.480 --> 08:06.910
Oh, but it's normal for them
to be under the same roof, right?

08:06.910 --> 08:09.720
A prisoner is a prisoner.

08:09.720 --> 08:15.260
If we go easy on them,
the men will let it get to their heads!

08:15.260 --> 08:16.490
W-What now?

08:16.490 --> 08:20.060
Is she going to start
another riot like before?

08:20.060 --> 08:22.900
M-Maybe we should inform
our captain or the vice...

08:22.900 --> 08:26.230
It's not like I'm going to do anything!

08:28.740 --> 08:30.370
Promise?

08:30.370 --> 08:32.870
You promised that you
would go to Dita's room?

08:32.870 --> 08:34.110
Yeah.

08:34.110 --> 08:36.880
I said it in the heat of the moment.

08:36.880 --> 08:39.350
I think it's all right.
Why don't you go visit her?

08:39.350 --> 08:41.080
Why don't you go then?

08:41.080 --> 08:44.350
You're the one that
made the promise, right?

08:44.350 --> 08:46.920
You've got to be kidding! I'm a guy!

08:46.920 --> 08:48.660
Why should I go to a woman's room?

08:48.660 --> 08:51.530
A man is someone
that keeps his promises.

08:51.530 --> 08:55.330
The old you would be adamant
about that part, I would think.

08:56.830 --> 08:59.730
I don't mean to break my promise.

08:59.730 --> 09:01.000
But...

09:01.000 --> 09:01.870
But?

09:01.870 --> 09:03.000
But what?

09:03.000 --> 09:06.570
I'm saying, what am I supposed
to do in a woman's room?

09:06.570 --> 09:08.800
What do we talk about?

09:11.280 --> 09:12.270
- True.
- True.

09:14.050 --> 09:16.420
I've detected a distress signal.

09:16.420 --> 09:17.520
Type?

09:17.520 --> 09:20.390
It's not from the Earth's fleet.

09:20.390 --> 09:22.560
Please wait. We've determined it.

09:22.560 --> 09:25.230
Its pattern is from the frontier era.

09:25.230 --> 09:26.460
What should we do?

09:26.460 --> 09:29.600
It smells fishy, but we
can't just leave them, right?

09:29.600 --> 09:30.600
Parfet!

09:30.600 --> 09:31.530
Yes!

09:31.530 --> 09:33.000
How's the Paksis doing?

09:33.000 --> 09:34.600
Staying alive, somehow.

09:34.600 --> 09:35.970
Roger.

09:35.970 --> 09:37.740
Young man!

09:37.740 --> 09:39.070
Break's over.

09:39.070 --> 09:41.940
Sure. I'll be right over.

09:41.940 --> 09:45.970
Now, what will come out of this?

09:51.490 --> 09:52.920
Wow, it's amazing!

09:52.920 --> 09:54.720
It's moving!

09:54.720 --> 09:56.060
We're in the last month.

09:56.060 --> 09:59.390
According to calculations,
they should separate at any moment.

09:59.390 --> 10:03.200
Separate? We call it "giving birth."

10:03.200 --> 10:05.870
Hey, where would you
like to have your baby?

10:05.870 --> 10:07.770
We don't have the facilities here.

10:07.770 --> 10:10.290
But then, considering it's a guy...

10:12.740 --> 10:14.010
I'm a doctor.

10:14.010 --> 10:17.950
I believe I'm done
learning about pregnancy.

10:17.950 --> 10:20.040
I'm still worried, ribbit.

10:22.080 --> 10:25.320
Doctor, can I have
something for my headache?

10:25.320 --> 10:26.590
What's wrong?

10:26.590 --> 10:29.790
I've been like this ever since
I had a strange dream this morning.

10:29.790 --> 10:31.190
A dream?

10:31.190 --> 10:34.130
Come to think, Hibiki mentioned
he had the same dream.

10:34.130 --> 10:37.300
The Paksis also seems to be acting up.

10:37.300 --> 10:38.960
Is there a connection?

10:40.970 --> 10:44.710
Never mind that!
Hurry up and give me the medicine!

10:44.710 --> 10:46.810
I-I'm sorry for yelling.

10:46.810 --> 10:48.380
I'll prepare it right away.

10:48.380 --> 10:50.170
Sit down right there.

10:54.720 --> 10:57.910
Your baby has grown.

11:00.150 --> 11:02.150
"Hello, Baby"

11:03.020 --> 11:05.390
The fact that a distress
signal is activated...

11:05.390 --> 11:08.460
means a battle at any
time may not be unexpected.

11:08.460 --> 11:12.500
Check the system conditions
more carefully than usual.

11:12.500 --> 11:13.990
Roger!

11:15.000 --> 11:18.540
Well, I guess this is an improvement.

11:18.540 --> 11:19.530
Huh?

11:30.850 --> 11:33.320
I want a baby.

11:34.390 --> 11:35.690
A baby?

11:35.690 --> 11:36.760
Yeah.

11:36.760 --> 11:38.060
W-What?

11:38.060 --> 11:40.230
You want me to be an ohma?

11:40.230 --> 11:42.260
No, it's not that.

11:42.260 --> 11:45.260
There's meaning in
making a baby with a guy!

11:46.800 --> 11:49.740
Making a baby with a man's seed.

11:49.740 --> 11:52.540
Think about going back
to Mejale with that news!

11:52.540 --> 11:54.880
The first woman to make
a baby with a male seed!

11:54.880 --> 11:57.940
It's the birth of a new heroine!

11:59.250 --> 12:01.820
Well, that's like you.

12:01.820 --> 12:04.520
So? How do you get the seed?

12:04.520 --> 12:05.790
Can you find out for me?

12:05.790 --> 12:07.880
Y-You want me to?

12:11.460 --> 12:14.600
Distress signal location
has been confirmed.

12:14.600 --> 12:16.200
Dread Team, go.

12:16.200 --> 12:17.030
Meia.

12:17.030 --> 12:19.830
We'll start a salvage operation
with the deli ships now.

12:19.830 --> 12:21.940
But we don't know
when the enemy will attack.

12:21.940 --> 12:23.140
Please guard them.

12:23.140 --> 12:24.130
Roger.

12:31.250 --> 12:33.240
That's some pretty heavy damage.

12:35.350 --> 12:38.250
I've confirmed a life sign.

12:38.250 --> 12:40.240
Someone escaped the harvest?

12:42.020 --> 12:43.460
All right, got it!

12:43.460 --> 12:45.620
That's the plan.

12:47.060 --> 12:49.060
What timing!

12:49.060 --> 12:51.000
Enemy signatures approaching.

12:51.000 --> 12:52.830
- Distance: 20,000!
- So they're here.

12:52.830 --> 12:55.270
I guess we really are outlaws.

12:55.270 --> 12:58.040
Well, that's more like a pirate.

12:58.040 --> 13:00.470
This is a new signal pattern.

13:00.470 --> 13:03.680
We can't get data
about the enemy fleet.

13:03.680 --> 13:06.410
It looks like they've launched
from a different flagship.

13:06.410 --> 13:09.720
The enemy seems to have
advanced quite a distance.

13:09.720 --> 13:12.250
Five of them are headed our way.

13:12.250 --> 13:14.920
That's no surprise, no matter
where we encounter them.

13:14.920 --> 13:17.930
If all five come at once,
we should run without a second thought!

13:17.930 --> 13:20.900
The Dread teams should
guard Gascogne's return.

13:20.900 --> 13:23.500
Parfet, can we raise the shields?

13:23.500 --> 13:26.130
I don't have complete control.

13:26.130 --> 13:27.770
It's still unstable!

13:27.770 --> 13:30.270
Looks like we have no time to stay idle.

13:30.270 --> 13:33.040
Meia, avoid unnecessary battle.

13:33.040 --> 13:35.610
As soon as the pod is retrieved,
we will depart.

13:35.610 --> 13:36.380
Roger.

13:36.380 --> 13:38.080
Oh, that's our vice-captain!

13:38.080 --> 13:39.780
What a wonderful decision!

13:39.780 --> 13:42.010
Oh, thanks...

13:52.390 --> 13:54.290
When'd they get under us?

13:57.360 --> 13:59.960
They're much faster
than the last set of cubes!

14:02.670 --> 14:06.010
The enemy ship is taking the pod
and returning to the flagship!

14:06.010 --> 14:08.410
They aren't after us?

14:08.410 --> 14:10.950
Then we really can't let them have it.

14:10.950 --> 14:15.450
That pod must be something
very important to Earth.

14:15.450 --> 14:17.890
We were the ones who got that first!

14:17.890 --> 14:19.410
I'll take it back!

14:23.760 --> 14:25.020
T-They're quick!

14:28.100 --> 14:29.000
We're combining.

14:29.000 --> 14:31.570
Let's get that pod back
and return to the Nirvana!

14:31.570 --> 14:32.550
Sure!

14:36.400 --> 14:38.610
Red... light...

14:38.610 --> 14:40.070
The pod!

14:40.070 --> 14:42.810
Get the pod and hurry
back to the Nirvana!

14:42.810 --> 14:45.010
S-Sure!

14:45.010 --> 14:47.000
I won't let you have it!

14:49.320 --> 14:51.490
Damn it!

14:51.490 --> 14:53.510
It's mine!

15:00.360 --> 15:02.730
Well? Pretty good, right?

15:02.730 --> 15:05.600
What are you saying,
coming out this late in the game?

15:05.600 --> 15:06.500
You know...

15:06.500 --> 15:08.600
W-What do you want?

15:08.600 --> 15:12.310
What will you give my baby?

15:12.310 --> 15:14.940
W-What stupid things
are you saying now?

15:14.940 --> 15:17.510
This is no time to be
doing that kind of stuff!

15:17.510 --> 15:19.350
Jura, head straight for the Nirvana.

15:19.350 --> 15:20.780
R-Roger.

15:20.780 --> 15:23.320
The enemy has entered observation mode.

15:23.320 --> 15:24.810
We'll use this time to...

15:29.660 --> 15:31.320
That light!

15:33.590 --> 15:34.720
W-What is it?

15:37.600 --> 15:40.470
W-What's going on now?

15:40.470 --> 15:43.000
Vandread Jura has separated.

15:43.000 --> 15:44.670
Separated? What do you mean?

15:44.670 --> 15:46.340
I'm not really sure...

15:46.340 --> 15:50.440
but that light interfered
and forced them to separate!

15:50.440 --> 15:52.450
What?

15:52.450 --> 15:53.850
Mr. Alien!

15:53.850 --> 15:55.680
Are you all right?

15:55.680 --> 15:57.780
H-Huh? Where did it go?

15:58.990 --> 15:59.790
There!

15:59.790 --> 16:01.650
Leave the target to me!

16:03.520 --> 16:06.520
Damn it, don't get in my way!

16:07.960 --> 16:09.620
Don't!

16:35.320 --> 16:36.790
How's that?

16:36.790 --> 16:39.160
We won't let them have it so easily!

16:39.160 --> 16:41.000
Right, Mr. Alien?

16:41.000 --> 16:43.100
Celebrate later.

16:43.100 --> 16:45.830
The enemy is approaching.
Hurry up and retreat!

16:45.830 --> 16:47.490
Roger!

16:56.040 --> 16:58.110
Hibiki! Dita!

16:58.110 --> 17:01.850
W-What is that?

17:01.850 --> 17:03.280
The right arm...

17:05.750 --> 17:08.120
Mr. Alien, this is...

17:09.890 --> 17:12.520
Are you saying that the
dream is going to come true?

17:15.230 --> 17:17.800
It hurts more than usual!

17:17.800 --> 17:20.070
Hey, engine room! What's going on?

17:20.070 --> 17:22.470
I want to know myself!

17:22.470 --> 17:25.570
It looks like we're being
affected by that red light.

17:25.570 --> 17:28.370
Yeah, it's as if we're scared of it.

17:31.350 --> 17:33.710
Pyoro, what's wrong with you now?

17:33.710 --> 17:35.580
It's very close.

17:35.580 --> 17:39.320
But it's a distinct existence.

17:39.320 --> 17:42.820
Dangerous to approach.
But they call for each other.

17:42.820 --> 17:45.990
I'm scared, but...

17:45.990 --> 17:47.590
What is it saying?

17:47.590 --> 17:49.030
It sounds like it's drunk.

17:49.030 --> 17:52.990
Really, it acts like a creature.

18:07.380 --> 18:08.480
What's going on?

18:08.480 --> 18:09.480
Damn it!

18:09.480 --> 18:10.820
It's not moving!

18:10.820 --> 18:13.520
Main enemy force is
approaching Vandread Dita!

18:13.520 --> 18:16.060
It looks like it's
going to collect the pod!

18:16.060 --> 18:18.790
Vandread Dita still isn't moving!

18:18.790 --> 18:23.060
With that red light, all it can
do is maintain its current form!

18:23.060 --> 18:25.960
Are you saying...
that's a new enemy weapon?

18:35.640 --> 18:37.300
Hibiki! Dita!

18:42.050 --> 18:43.710
It's over!

18:45.250 --> 18:49.220
Dreams are for when we're asleep.

18:49.220 --> 18:51.760
While my eyes are open...

18:51.760 --> 18:55.750
I won't ever let you have it your way!

19:03.370 --> 19:04.640
We did it!

19:04.640 --> 19:05.810
Let's go!

19:05.810 --> 19:07.470
Right!

19:11.310 --> 19:14.180
We have no time to deal with dreams!

19:27.730 --> 19:30.430
He still is a reckless guy.

19:30.430 --> 19:32.600
We did it! We did it! We did it!

19:32.600 --> 19:34.370
We win!

19:34.370 --> 19:36.370
There's really nothing
to be scared of...

19:36.370 --> 19:38.470
...if we combine our powers!

19:38.470 --> 19:41.340
Isn't that right, Mr. Alien?

19:41.340 --> 19:43.580
You're really...

19:43.580 --> 19:45.280
What?

19:45.280 --> 19:48.920
N-Nothing.

19:48.920 --> 19:52.990
I still don't know what to talk about.

19:52.990 --> 19:55.060
What did you just say?

19:55.060 --> 19:56.760
Come on, say it again.

19:56.760 --> 19:59.190
Shut up. Just talking to myself.

19:59.190 --> 20:00.890
But it makes me wonder!

20:00.890 --> 20:02.490
When I say shut up, shut up!

20:10.500 --> 20:12.530
And... there.

20:19.780 --> 20:21.250
There's a girl inside!

20:21.250 --> 20:22.380
Is it an alien?

20:22.380 --> 20:25.050
Sorry. It should be a human,
just like us.

20:25.050 --> 20:26.950
I see...

20:26.950 --> 20:28.690
Hey, let me see, too!

20:28.690 --> 20:30.380
Let me see!

20:32.030 --> 20:32.990
Is she alive?

20:32.990 --> 20:35.200
The life support system
is functioning properly.

20:35.200 --> 20:38.820
Damn it, let me see!

20:42.570 --> 20:44.140
She came to!

20:44.140 --> 20:46.440
Who came to...

20:55.750 --> 20:58.080
I thought I was gonna die.

21:02.560 --> 21:05.060
W-What is this?

21:05.060 --> 21:06.690
You.

21:06.690 --> 21:08.680
You were the one that saved me!

21:10.100 --> 21:13.170
